+# RAPTOR branch `blp-bbh`: changes and upstream defects
+
+Branch `blp-bbh` of RAPTOR (Bronzwaer et al. 2018, A&A 613, A2; Bronzwaer et
+al. 2020, A&A 641, A126) forks upstream `main` at
+`b91e937b7b746eb24992b6c1dd8831c5dea0cef1` (2024-08-12). It runs RAPTOR with
+the geometry, camera, march, plasma model and Stokes convention of
+BlackLightPlus, so that images of binary-black-hole AthenaK snapshots can be
+compared code to code. Branch `blp-reader` (the AthenaK data layer) is merged
+into it at `e0f0570`.
+
+Every change is either behind a compile-time switch whose default keeps the
+upstream behaviour, or is a fix of an upstream defect. With every switch at its
+default the upstream synthetic BHAC image is bitwise identical to `b91e937`
+(BlackLightPlus `results/blp/raptor/evidence/R05/r01_bitwise.json`).
+
+The comparison that uses this branch, its protocol and results are in the
+BlackLightPlus repository: `docs/src/validation.md`,
+`results/blp/raptor/report.md`, and the patch series of this branch in
+`results/blp/raptor/patches/` (rebuild recipe in `results/blp/raptor/fork.md`).
+Evidence paths below are relative to `results/blp/raptor/` in that repository.
+
+## Switches
+
+Defaults are those of `src/functions.h`; `model/blp_analytic/definitions.h`
+sets the values in the third column.
+
+| Switch | Default | `blp_analytic` | Effect |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `metric == SKS` (id 9) | — | on | M1 superposed Kerr–Schild binary from `bbh.in` (`$RAPTOR_BBH`) |
+| `SKS_CONNECTION` | `SKS_CONN_FD` | FD | M2a finite-difference connection; `SKS_CONN_ANALYTIC` selects M2b |
+| `STEP_BBH` | 0 | 1 | M3 march control, termination and transfer sample set |
+| `CAMERA_PP` | 0 | 1 | M4 plane-parallel camera at `cam_dist` |
+| `EMIS_BLP` | 0 | 1 | M7 BlackLightPlus thermal coefficients with the $j_P\le j_I$ and $\alpha_P\le\alpha_I$ rescales |
+| `STOKES_IAU` | 0 | 1 | M8 camera readout in the IEEE/IAU convention |
+| `EMIS_MODEL` | 0 | 1 | coefficients supplied by the model (`model_evaluate_coeffs`; analytic scenes) |
+| `POL_KEEP_I` | 0 | 1 | polarized readout keeps the transported $I$ of pixels whose polarized invariant never passes the activation threshold (D11) |
+| `POL_SOLVER_LD85` | 0 | 0 | M11 exact constant-coefficient polarized step instead of `check_stiffness` → RK4 / trapezoid |
+| `ATHK_UPSTREAM_PLASMA` | 0 | — | `model/athenak` only (`model_definitions.h`): the `model/bhac` plasma decode on AthenaK data |
+
+`bbh.in` holds `nholes`, `mass`, `spin`, `center1`, `center2`, `C`, `nmax`,
+`escape`, `horizon_eps`, `capture_redshift` and `cam_dist`.
+
