+## Upstream defects
+
+Locations are at `b91e937`. "Fixed" means fixed on this branch; "reported"
+means documented and avoided in the comparison, with upstream code unchanged.
+The last column marks a defect as a candidate for an upstream fix, as opposed
+to a convention that only matters for matching BlackLightPlus.
+
+| Id | Defect | Location | Symptom | Status | Evidence | Upstream |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| D1 | CKS metric regularisers: $1/(\Sigma+10^{-3})$ and $l_z=z/(r+10^{-3})$ in $g_{\mu\nu}$, but $l_z=z/r$ in $g^{\mu\nu}$ | `src/metric.c:183-184`, `:195`; `:371-372` | $g\,g^{-1}\ne\mathbb 1$: $7.3\times10^{-4}$ at $r=1.3$–3, $1.2\times10^{-4}$ at 5–10, $3.4\times10^{-5}$ at 10–40; finite-difference $\Gamma$ off by up to $1.8\times10^{-3}$; CKS Kerr rays converge at order 0.9 instead of 4 | reported; M1 is a separate metric without regularisers | `evidence/R04/metric.json` (`kerr_upstream_cks`) | yes |
+| D2 | Finite-difference Christoffel step relative to the coordinate, $h=10^{-4}\max(\lvert x^i\rvert,10^{-6})$ | `src/metric.c:461-485` | $h\to10^{-10}$ near a coordinate plane, about six digits lost there; 16 metric calls per right-hand side | fixed for SKS (M2a, `87883ff`): $\Gamma$ within $6.1\times10^{-11}$ of AD; CKS unchanged | `evidence/R04/metric.json`, `evidence/R09/metric.json` | yes |
+| D3 | Electron temperature with a fixed $(\gamma-1)=1/3$: $\Theta_e=(u/\rho)\tfrac13(m_p/m_e)/(1+R)$ while $\beta$ uses the dump's $\gamma$ | `model/bhac/model.c:1184`, `:1186` | $0.75\times$ the pressure-based $\Theta_e$ for $\gamma=13/9$; with the $\Theta_e\in[10^{-3},100]$ and $r<1$, $r>50$ cuts and floors (`:1022`, `:1025`, `:1070`, `:1138-1139`, `:1191-1193`) the stock leg is 43–47% fainter on s455 | reported; available as M6s for the stock leg | `evidence/R07/metrics.json` (`report_legs`) | yes (the $\gamma$ inconsistency) |
+| D4 | Trilinear interpolation weights measured from the lower cell face while the data sit at cell centres | `model/bhac/model.c:885-926` (`:906`); centres `:312` | samples shifted by half a cell | reported; not on the compared path (M5 samples at cell centres) | — | yes |
+| D5 | ASCII image writer truncates `(x-corner)/dx - 0.5` | `src/camera.c:261-262` | on the synthetic BHAC image 8278 of 10000 rows unique; ASCII flux 1.1% high | reported; images read from HDF5 | — | yes |
+| D6 | Planck function as `exp(hν/kT) - 1` | `src/pol_emission.c:54-60` | at 230 GHz $h\nu/kT\approx1.9\times10^{-9}/\Theta_e$: about half the double-precision digits of the Kirchhoff absorptivities lost | fixed in M7 only (`expm1`); native fits unchanged | — | yes |
+| D7 | Camera readout basis: `cam_up` $=-\hat z$ with the Kerr observer gives $e_{(1)}$ west, $e_{(2)}$ north | `src/pol_rte_integrator.c:709-725` (`:712`) | $Q=-Q_{\rm IAU}$, $U=-U_{\rm IAU}$, $V=V_{\rm IEEE}$ on every orientation slab and on the ring, against the IEEE/IAU convention stated in Bronzwaer et al. (2020) | fixed behind `STOKES_IAU` (`b9d7443`): ring within $7\times10^{-8}$ of BlackLightPlus | `evidence/R02/orientation.json` | report the convention mismatch |
+| D8 | Unpolarized transfer drops the emission of absorption-free segments: `if (K_inv == 0) Icurrent = Ii;` | `src/rte_integrator.c:125-126` | Gold et al. (2020) tests T1–T3 (no absorption) render blank | fixed, unconditional (`aaa32ce`): adds $j\,ds$; T1–T5 then agree with BlackLightPlus to $L_1\le1.6\times10^{-8}$ | `evidence/R02/analytic.json` | yes |
+| D9 | `check_stiffness` evaluates the RK4 amplification with $\tau=+\lambda\,dl$ (wrong sign, without `C_CONST`) against 0.99 | `src/pol_rte_integrator.c:360-407` (`:375-378`, `:400-404`) | every absorbing segment takes the implicit trapezoid (100% of test segments), second order (measured 2.00); median per-segment phase error 0.20 at Faraday depth 1–10, 0.32 at 10–300 | reported; M11 is the exact alternative | `evidence/R07/polstep.json` | yes |
+| D10 | $\rho_Q$ thermal: $K_1(1/\Theta_e)/K_2(1/\Theta_e)$ is 0/0 once GSL $K_n$ underflows | `src/pol_emission.c:133` ($\rho_V$ already guards $K_0/K_2$ at `:220-227`) | NaN for $\Theta_e<1.26\times10^{-3}$ (7353 of 110808 test values); a NaN clears `POLARIZATION_ACTIVE` and blanks the pixel: 20%, 30%, 100% of the s455 flux lost at $i=17^\circ,60^\circ,90^\circ$ | fixed, unconditional (`d01fc9a` test, `502d876`): ratio → 1 when $K_2=0$; 0 of 110808 non-finite | `evidence/R07/native_cold.txt` | yes |
