+| D15 | `setup.sh -g` compares the default `GRID="smr"` with `"SMR"`/`"AMR"` | `setup.sh:9`, `:124`, `:131` | the flag has no effect; `AMR 0 / SMR 1` of `definitions.h:49-50` always hold | reported | — | yes |
+| D16 | `thetadot_prev` read uninitialised in the $\theta$-turn order cut, which also uses `photon_u[6]` ($k^y$ in CKS) | `src/gr_integrator.c:340`, `:386-391` | undefined behaviour; the cut never fires at `max_order = 100` | removed under `STEP_BBH` (M3) | — | yes |
+
+Upstream limitations that the comparison works around: the polarized march
+runs only inside `RT_OUTER_CUTOFF` = 50 (`src/pol_rte_integrator.c:780`,
+raised to $1.1\times10^3$ by M9); $k$ is re-nulled when $\lvert k\cdot k\rvert>10^{-6}$
+at $r>2$ (`:771-772`, off under M3); $j_P$ and $\alpha_P$ are rescaled by
+$1/(p+0.005)$ (`:345-356`) and $\lvert P\rvert$ is renormalised (`:653-664`),
+both bypassed by M11; images are square with a multiple of 10 pixels
+(`src/camera.c:28-33`); the native step control and termination refer to one
+hole at the origin.
+
+## Test drivers
+
+`tests/build_tests.sh <dir>` builds, against `model/blp_analytic`:
+`coeff_table` (coefficient table), `metric_dump` and `metric_dump_cks` (metric
+and connection), `ray_dump` and the `ccall` libraries `libraptor_sks_fd.so`,
+`libraptor_sks_an.so`, `libraptor_cks.so` (rays and camera),
+`libraptor_rt_pol.so`, `libraptor_rt_unpol.so` (one image point through camera,
+march and transfer), `libraptor_pol_step.so` (one polarized segment, native and
+M11 step) and `native_cold` (finiteness of the upstream thermal fits for cold
+electrons). `model/athenak/tests/athenak_probe.c` and `fluid_probe.c` probe the
+AthenaK data layer and `get_fluid_params` on the binary metric.
